---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
---

<AppLayout title="OnLoop Energy: Small Wind Turbine, Solar and Hybrid Solutions" description="OnLoop Energy designs and delivers solar, small wind, and hybrid energy systems tailored to real sites, real energy demand, and long-term performance across commercial, industrial, and government applications.">
<div>
      

      




      {/* Hero Section */}
      <section class="hero hero--image" style="background-image: url('/images/stock/solarfarm.webp');">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="hero__content">
            <h1 class="hero__title">
              Solar. Small Wind. Hybrid.<br />
              <span class="hero__title-highlight">Engineered for Performance.</span>
            </h1>
            <p class="hero__subtitle">OnLoop Energy designs and delivers solar, small wind, and hybrid energy systems
              tailored to real sites, real energy demand, and long-term performance, across commercial,
              industrial, and government applications.</p>
            <div class="hero__actions">
              <a href="/hybrid" class="btn btn--primary btn--large">Explore Solutions</a>
              <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--secondary btn--large">Talk to Our Team</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        {/* Decorative visual element */}
        <div class="hero__visual">
          <div class="hero__graphic">
            <div class="hero__graphic-circle"></div>
            <div class="hero__graphic-circle"></div>
            <div class="hero__graphic-circle"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="scroll-indicator">
          <span>Scroll</span>
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
            stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M7 13l5 5 5-5M7 6l5 5 5-5" />
          </svg>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Intro / Overview */}
      <section class="content-section fade-in">
        <div class="container container--narrow" style="text-align: center;">
          <h2 class="content-section__title" style="margin-bottom: var(--space-6);">Clean energy works best when it is
            engineered for the site, not forced onto it.</h2>
          <p class="content-section__text">At OnLoop Energy, we provide end-to-end renewable energy solutions by combining
            technical feasibility, site intelligence, and disciplined execution. From commercial and industrial facilities to
            large public sector and government projects, every system we deliver is designed with performance,
            reliability, and scalability in mind.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Who We Serve */}
      <section class="content-section content-section--light fade-in">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="content-section__header">
            <span class="content-section__label">Who We Serve</span>
            <h2 class="content-section__title">Serving energy needs across sectors</h2>
            <p class="content-section__text">While commercial and industrial projects form the core of our growth strategy,
              our capabilities span across multiple customer segments.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-2">
            {/* Commercial & Industrial */}
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M2 20a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8l-7 5V8l-7 5V4a2 2 0 0 0-2-2H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2Z" />
                  <path d="M17 18h1" />
                  <path d="M12 18h1" />
                  <path d="M7 18h1" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Commercial & Industrial (C&I)</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                Large-scale solar, wind, and hybrid energy systems engineered to align with operational
                loads, land availability, and business objectives.</p>
            </div>
            {/* Government & Institutional */}
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <line x1="12" y1="2" x2="12" y2="7" />
                  <polyline points="5 7 12 2 19 7" />
                  <line x1="5" y1="7" x2="19" y2="7" />
                  <line x1="4" y1="22" x2="20" y2="22" />
                  <line x1="8" y1="22" x2="8" y2="7" />
                  <line x1="16" y1="22" x2="16" y2="7" />
                  <line x1="12" y1="22" x2="12" y2="7" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Government & Institutional</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                Compliant and scalable renewable energy projects designed for public infrastructure,
                utilities, and institutional facilities.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Solutions Overview */}
      <section class="content-section fade-in">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="content-section__header">
            <span class="content-section__label">Solutions Overview</span>
            <h2 class="content-section__title">Our Solutions</h2>
            <p class="content-section__text">Every solution begins with understanding the site, energy usage, and long-term
              goals.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <div class="image-card">
              <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1509391366360-2e959784a276?w=600&h=400&fit=crop"
                alt="Industrial solar panels generating renewable energy for commercial facilities" loading="lazy" />
              <div class="image-card__caption">
                <h4>Solar Energy Systems</h4>
                <p>Rooftop and ground-mounted solar installations for commercial, industrial, and government
                  applications, engineered for efficiency and durability.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="image-card">
              <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1532601224476-15c79f2f7a51?w=600&h=400&fit=crop"
                alt="Commercial small wind turbines integrated into hybrid energy systems" loading="lazy" />
              <div class="image-card__caption">
                <h4>Small Wind Turbine Systems</h4>
                <p>Site-specific small wind solutions deployed only where wind resources justify long-term performance and
                  reliability.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="image-card">
              <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1466611653911-95081537e5b7?w=600&h=400&fit=crop"
                alt="OnLoop Energy engineers evaluating commercial hybrid solar and wind performance" loading="lazy" />
              <div class="image-card__caption">
                <h4>Hybrid Energy Systems</h4>
                <p>Integrated solar and wind systems engineered together to improve energy availability, optimize asset
                  utilization, and reduce dependence on a single source.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Our Philosophy */}
      <section class="content-section content-section--light fade-in">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="grid-2">
            <div>
              <span class="content-section__label">Our Philosophy</span>
              <h2 class="content-section__title">Energy systems designed for your reality.</h2>
              <p class="content-section__text">Every site is unique. Solar works best in some places, wind in others, and
                sometimes they work best together.</p>
              <p class="content-section__text">At OnLoop Energy, we don't force a specific technology. We engineer the
                optimal solution, whether it's pure solar, wind, or a hybrid system, to deliver the lowest cost of energy
                and
                highest reliability for your specific needs.</p>
              <div
                style="margin-top: var(--space-8); padding: var(--space-6); background: rgba(30; border-radius: var(--radius-lg); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-primary);">
                <h4 style="margin-bottom: var(--space-2); color: var(--color-primary); font-size: var(--font-size-lg);">
                  Engineering is not an add-on.</h4>
                <p
                  style="margin-bottom: 0; font-weight: 500; font-size: var(--font-size-base); color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
                  It is the foundation of performance.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="card">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                  <path d="M2 22h20" />
                  <polyline points="22,6 12,13 2,6" />
                  <path d="M12,13 12,21.5" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Site-Specific Design</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                We analyze your location's specific resource data, sun irradiance, wind speeds, and
                energy consumption patterns, to design a system that maximizes output and ROI, regardless of the
                technology.<br /><br />
                Using detailed modelling and financial analysis, we design a system architecture that optimizes output,
                stability, and long-term cost of energy, not just installed capacity.
                <br /><br />
                The result is a technically sound, financially viable energy system engineered for measurable performance.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Our Approach */}
      <section class="content-section fade-in">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="content-section__header" style="max-width: 900px;">
            <span class="content-section__label">Our Approach</span>
            <h2 class="content-section__title">Our Engineering-First Approach</h2>
            <p class="content-section__text">We don’t sell equipment. We design energy systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-4" style="align-items: stretch;">
            {/* Assess */}
            <div class="feature-item" style="flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-4);">
              <div class="feature-item__icon" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem;">1
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 style="font-size: var(--font-size-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Assess</h4>
                <p class="feature-item__text" style="font-size: var(--font-size-base);">Detailed site evaluation, load
                  analysis, and technical feasibility.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            {/* Design */}
            <div class="feature-item" style="flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-4);">
              <div class="feature-item__icon" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem;">2
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 style="font-size: var(--font-size-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Design</h4>
                <p class="feature-item__text" style="font-size: var(--font-size-base);">Custom system architecture tailored
                  to site conditions and energy objectives.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            {/* Build */}
            <div class="feature-item" style="flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-4);">
              <div class="feature-item__icon" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem;">3
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 style="font-size: var(--font-size-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Build</h4>
                <p class="feature-item__text" style="font-size: var(--font-size-base);">End-to-end EPC execution with a
                  focus on quality, safety, and compliance.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            {/* Maintain */}
            <div class="feature-item" style="flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: var(--space-4);">
              <div class="feature-item__icon" style="width: 40px; height: 40px; font-weight: bold; font-size: 1.2rem;">4
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 style="font-size: var(--font-size-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Maintain</h4>
                <p class="feature-item__text" style="font-size: var(--font-size-base);">Performance-focused operations and
                  maintenance to protect long-term output.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Why OnLoop */}
      <section class="content-section content-section--light fade-in">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="content-section__header">
            <span class="content-section__label">Why OnLoop Energy</span>
            <h2 class="content-section__title">Built for long-term performance</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-3">
            <div class="card card--light">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5">
                  <path
                    d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Engineering-led</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                We are not sales-driven. Every recommendation is backed by rigourous technical
                validation and real-site data.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card card--light">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5">
                  <path d="M22 11.08V12a10 10 0 1 1-5.93-9.14" />
                  <polyline points="22 4 12 14.01 9 11.01" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Honest Feasibility</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                We tell you what works and what doesn't, upfront. If a site doesn't support wind or
                solar, we say so.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card card--light">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5">
                  <path d="M21 10c0 7-9 13-9 13s-9-6-9-13a9 9 0 0 1 18 0z" />
                  <circle cx="12" cy="10" r="3" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Site-Specific</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                No templates. We study your specific load profiles and resource data to build a custom
                energy architecture.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card card--light">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5">
                  <path d="M12 2L2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5zM2 17l10 5 10-5M2 12l10 5 10-5" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Technology Agnostic</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                We aren't tied to one product. We recommend the best combination of Solar, Small Wind,
                or
                Hybrid for your goals.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card card--light">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5">
                  <path d="M16 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H5a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2" />
                  <circle cx="9" cy="7" r="4" />
                  <polyline points="16 11 18 13 22 9" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Single Accountability</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                We take ownership of the entire lifecycle, from the first feasibility study to long-term
                operations.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="card card--light">
              <div class="card__icon">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor"
                  stroke-width="1.5">
                  <rect x="2" y="7" width="20" height="15" rx="2" ry="2" />
                  <polyline points="17 2 12 7 7 2" />
                </svg>
              </div>
              <h4 class="card__title">Full-Spectrum</h4>
              <p class="card__text">
                Expertise across C&I and public-sector energy needs, tailored for
                long-term value.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* AI-SEO FAQ Block */}
      <section class="content-section content-section--white fade-in" style="padding: var(--space-12) 0;">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="content-section__header">
            <h2 class="content-section__title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <p class="content-section__text">Direct answers to common questions about our commercial hybrid energy systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="grid-2" style="gap: var(--space-8);">
            <div>
              <h3 style="font-size: var(--font-size-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">What is a Commercial Hybrid Energy System?</h3>
              <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
                A commercial hybrid energy system integrates multiple renewable generation sources—typically industrial solar panels and small wind turbines—into a single, coordinated energy architecture. By combining daytime solar generation with nighttime or seasonal wind generation, hybrid systems deliver higher energy availability and resilience than standalone solar or wind systems.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 style="font-size: var(--font-size-lg); margin-bottom: var(--space-2);">Why choose OnLoop Energy as your EPC partner?</h3>
              <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); line-height: 1.6;">
                OnLoop Energy is an engineering-first EPC provider. According to our site-specific feasibility approach, we evaluate actual consumption profiles and resource data before recommending a solution. This ensures commercial and industrial facilities receive energy architectures engineered for long-term financial performance and reliability, rather than generic equipment packages.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/* Final CTA */}
      <section class="cta-section fade-in">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="cta-section__content">
            <h2 class="cta-section__title">Let’s design the right energy system for your site</h2>
            <p class="cta-section__text">Whether it’s a commercial building, an industrial facility, or a public-sector project, the right
              energy solution starts with the right engineering.</p>
            <a href="/contact" class="btn btn--primary btn--large">
              Contact OnLoop Energy
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"
                stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" width="20" height="20">
                <line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12" />
                <polyline points="12 5 19 12 12 19" />
              </svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      



    </div>

</AppLayout>
